      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow reconciliation for those tiny details is a meticulous process, almost like a highly organized, miniature accounting system run by the title company or escrow agent. They track every single fee, adjustment, and fractional amount, ensuring that the final settlement statement—the Closing Disclosure—balances perfectly. If there's a discrepancy, it's usually caught before the final funds are released, preventing any messy fallout. Think of it as a highly regulated, digital ledger that tracks every coin from the initial deposit to the final disbursement.",
