    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the explanation. i guess i'm just worried about the sheer volume of those little transactions though. like, if you have dozens or hundreds of these tiny, micro-adjustments and small bits of money all swirling around in the agent's accounts at once, it feels like there's a lot of room for something to slip through the cracks. it's like all these little pieces are just hiding in the corners of the ledger or getting lost in the shuffle. is there actually a way to make sure none of those small bits just... vanish? like, how do they keep an eye on the \"small stuff\" so it doesn't just get nibbled away or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
